{{define "run-test"}}
<section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Deterministic black-box proof</p><h1>Run test</h1><p>Review the target, pipeline mode, and mutation scope. The harness runs its rule-schema and reserved-label preflight automatically.</p></section>
{{if .Error}}<div class="notice notice--error" role="alert">{{.Error}}</div>{{end}}
<section class="panel run-panel">
  <h2>Run a correlation scenario</h2>
  <form method="post" action="/runs" class="form-grid">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">
    <label>Target<select name="target_id" required>{{range .Targets}}<option value="{{.ID}}">{{.DisplayName}} — {{.BaseURL}}</option>{{end}}</select></label>
    <label>Pattern<select name="pattern" required>{{range .Scenarios}}<option value="{{.Pattern}}">{{.Pattern}} — {{len .Cases}} cases</option>{{end}}</select></label>
    <label>Pipeline mode<select name="pipeline_mode" required><option value="phase_b_dispatch">Phase B — audit and dispatch</option><option value="phase_a_audit_only">Phase A — audit only (cannot pass dispatch assertions)</option></select></label>
    <div class="form-actions"><button class="primary-button" type="submit">Start run</button></div>
  </form>
</section>
<section class="panel run-panel">
  <h2>Run the webhook receiver scenario</h2>
  <p>The bounded Flood scenario uses the pinned <code>corrtest_ordinary_v1</code> webhook mapping, Native Alertmanager, and the normal callback path. Configure the target’s ordinary webhook binding before running.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/runs/webhook" class="form-grid">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">
    <label>Target<select name="target_id" required>{{range .Targets}}<option value="{{.ID}}">{{.DisplayName}} — {{.BaseURL}}</option>{{end}}</select></label>
    <label>Pipeline mode<select name="pipeline_mode" required><option value="phase_b_dispatch">Phase B — audit and dispatch</option><option value="phase_a_audit_only">Phase A — audit only</option></select></label>
    <div class="form-actions"><button class="primary-button" type="submit">Start webhook receiver scenario</button></div>
  </form>
</section>
<section class="panel run-panel">
  <h2>Run a saved scenario</h2>
  <p>Saved custom scenarios can also run from the browser, including other receiver fixtures supported by OSCAR Test Console.</p>
  {{if .ImportedScenarios}}<form method="post" action="/runs/saved" class="form-grid">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">
    <label>Target<select name="target_id" required>{{range .Targets}}<option value="{{.ID}}">{{.DisplayName}} — {{.BaseURL}}</option>{{end}}</select></label>
    <label>Saved scenario<select name="scenario_id" required>{{range .ImportedScenarios}}<option value="{{.ID}}">{{.Name}}</option>{{end}}</select></label>
    <label>Pipeline mode<select name="pipeline_mode" required><option value="phase_b_dispatch">Phase B — audit and dispatch</option><option value="phase_a_audit_only">Phase A — audit only</option></select></label>
    <div class="form-actions"><button class="primary-button" type="submit">Start saved scenario</button></div>
  </form>{{else}}<p>No saved scenarios yet. <a href="/scenarios">Open Scenario workbench</a>.</p>{{end}}
</section>
<section class="panel run-panel">
  <h2>Run an SNMP trap receiver check</h2>
  <p>Sends one H3C Smart Link problem trap and its matching clear through the target’s UDP trap receiver, then checks the normalized Alert History. The generated mapping <code>1.3.6.1.4.1.25506.2.147.2</code> must already be installed. This is a bounded functional check, not a throughput test.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/runs/trap" class="form-grid">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">
    <label>Target<select name="target_id" required>{{range .Targets}}<option value="{{.ID}}">{{.DisplayName}} — {{.BaseURL}}</option>{{end}}</select><small>The trap goes to this target’s hostname.</small></label>
    <label>SNMP UDP port<input name="trap_port" type="number" min="1" max="65535" value="162" required></label>
    <p class="muted">The SNMP community is read from <code>CORRTEST_SNMP_COMMUNITY</code> on the OSCAR Test Console host; it is never stored in the run.</p>
    <div class="form-actions"><button class="primary-button" type="submit">Start SNMP receiver check</button></div>
  </form>
</section>
<section class="panel run-panel">
  <h2>Run an SNMP load test</h2>
  <p>These are real alerts: the target’s enabled rules can send notifications or create tickets. A passing run checks mapped History identities and their resolved state; it does not prove delivery of every UDP packet or attribute resolution to a specific clear packet.</p>
  <p>Send a repeatable mix of real migrated problem traps, repeated alarms and delayed clears. Each selected family must pass a problem/clear preflight before load begins. Uses existing mappings and normal OSCAR routing.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/runs/trap-load" class="form-grid">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">
    <label>Target<select name="target_id" required>{{range .Targets}}<option value="{{.ID}}">{{.DisplayName}} — {{.BaseURL}}</option>{{end}}</select></label>
    <label>SNMP UDP port<input name="trap_port" type="number" min="1" max="65535" value="162" required></label>
    <label>Trap mix<select name="profile" required>
      <option value="mixed">Mixed: DHCPv6 40%, DHCPv4 30%, AAA 20%, address pool 10%</option>
      <option value="dhcpv6-limit">Juniper DHCPv6 interface limit exceeded / abated</option>
      <option value="dhcp-limit">Juniper DHCP interface limit exceeded / abated</option>
      <option value="aaa-server">Juniper authentication server disabled / enabled</option>
      <option value="address-pool">Juniper address pool high / abate threshold</option>
    </select><small>Mix percentages apply to new problem identities.</small></label>
    <label>Target local sends per second<input name="rate" type="number" min="1" max="25" value="5" required></label>
    <label>Nominal offer duration (seconds)<input name="duration" type="number" min="10" max="600" value="60" required></label>
    <label>Minimum time before clear (seconds)<input name="clear_delay" type="number" min="1" max="120" value="30" required></label>
    <label>History drain timeout (seconds)<input name="drain_timeout" type="number" min="10" max="1800" value="300" required></label>
    <p class="muted">Problems, repeats and clears share the local-send budget. Packet emission and arrival can vary. The sender allows scheduling lag of one second or 5% of elapsed offer time, then stops if exceeded. Preflight is separate. Remaining clears continue at the same rate after the offer window; cancellation stops new problems and attempts clears for owned problems without a prior clear attempt. Ambiguous sends are not replayed. Credentials use CORRTEST_SNMP_COMMUNITY on the OSCAR Test Console host.</p>
    <p class="muted">Results include the packet ledger, sender timing and exact History identities. A local UDP send is not a receiver acknowledgement. This test alone does not verify repeated-packet receipt, outbound notifications, UI/task responsiveness or capacity.</p>
    <div class="form-actions"><button class="primary-button" type="submit">Start SNMP load test</button></div>
  </form>
</section>
<section class="panel run-panel"><h2>Built-in coverage</h2><div class="data-table-wrapper"><table><caption>Positive and negative scenarios</caption><thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Scenario</th><th>Cases</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{range .Scenarios}}<tr><td><code>{{.Pattern}}</code></td><td>{{.Name}}</td><td>{{len .Cases}}</td></tr>{{end}}</tbody></table></div></section>
{{end}}
